Installation of the Docker on the Ubuntus Ec2 instance

1.Update the system

>> sudo apt update
>> sudo apt upgrade -y

2. Install the required packages

>> sudo apt install  -y ca-certificate curl

3.Add Docker's official GPG key

>> sudo install -m 0755 -d /etc/apt/keyrings

>> sudo curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg \
  -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.asc

>> sudo chmod a+r /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.asc


4. Add the Docker official repository 

>> echo \
  "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/docker.asc] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu \
  $(. /etc/os-release && echo "${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-$VERSION_CODENAME}") stable" | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null


5. Update the package index

>> sudo apt update

6. Install the latest Docker Engine 

>> sudo apt install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin


7. Verify the installation

>>  sudo docker --version
>>  sudo docker compose version
>>  sudo systemctl status docker

8. Allow the ubuntu user to run the Docker without  sudo 

>> sudo usermod -aG docker ubuntu

apply the group change :
>> newgrp docker

8.Test the docker 

>> docker run hello-world
>> docker ps
